  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively point toward temperature-dependent ordering, precipitation, dislocation obstruction, and interface-controlled ductility. Most notably, R3 establishes 600 °C annealing in a closely related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloy, R7 connects thermal disruption of order to reduced dislocation resistance, and R10 shows in a closely related FCC/B2 alloy that interface structure and stress concentration strongly control ductility. However, none identifies L12 ordering near Ni3Al stoichiometry, jagged FCC/B2 boundaries, elevated APBE and restricted cross-slip, or the specific 600-to-750 °C ductile-brittle-ductile reversal. Reconstructing that coupled mechanism and non-monotonic response would therefore require a substantial new idea."
